<panel time_reactive="true">
    <module>system/prisc+x pal/main_module.pal</module>
    <interact src="pieces/apps/player_app/interact_relay.txt" />
    <!-- REAL ARCHITECTURE CORRECTION (2026-08-30, direct instruction:
         "isn't it only that actual 2d/3d screen {interact screen}
         needs to be blitted? everything else can be just a typical hq
         window") - File/Desk/Close moved OUT of this legacy layout
         entirely, back to being real khtpm Elems in
         run_pchq_board_mode() itself (same real nav_index/focus/CSS
         system every other hq window uses - db-hq/chat-hai/events-hq).
         They still ultimately dispatch through this SAME real KEY:5/
         KEY:6/KEY:7 relay (bv_menu_input.c's own key=='5'/'6'/'7'
         handlers, unchanged, proven working) - khtpm's own Elems just
         call pchq_append_key() directly on click/Enter instead of
         this layout rendering a button for the legacy engine's own
         click-hit-testing to find. This board_viewer.chtpm is once
         again ONLY the real, legacy-native "Interact Mode" button -
         the one real piece of UI that genuinely has to stay
         legacy-owned (camera/selector nav is entirely internal to this
         engine's own INTERACT state machine - see this button's own
         header comment below). -->
    <!-- Real, hand-written onClick="INTERACT" button - the RESERVED
         command string chtpm_parser_pal.c itself special-cases (NOT
         reachable via a dynamically-generated ${piece_methods} row,
         which always becomes onClick="KEY:N" instead - confirmed via
         direct code read of the parser's own method-button-generation
         branch). Exact same convention as mutaclysm's own real,
         working game.chtpm:7 "Control Hero" button - see
         &.widgits/interact-fix-widget.txt for the full investigation.
         The engine itself (not this project's own ops) handles the
         mode flag, raw arrow-key relay into interact_relay.txt, ESC-
         exit, and the [>]->[^] focus-glyph swap - all natively. -->
    <button label="Interact Mode (camera + selector)" onClick="INTERACT" /><br/>
    <text label="${game_map}" /><br/>
    ${piece_methods}
</panel>
